 also come  back to that  but you've got that initially and then  troy levitt  doesn't help and then about a week  after stuff with him was started  hitting headlines the leak about  the ability to create trans characters  in the character creator comes out  i was honestly suspicious of it it  felt like a pr move and part of me  really did think i even tweeted about it  at the time  that this felt like damage control  this felt like the kind of decision that  would have been made from somebody who  knew that the thing was in the game  was looking at the bad press realized  that this  might conceivably help but that it would  look bad if it was a formal press  release because then it would be clear  that it was just being put out into the  public  sphere because they needed it for damage  control  i'm less inclined to think that now even  though i did initially  uh for a couple also let me be clear at  no point  even when i was being slightly  conspiratorial about it at no point did  i believe that it was  put into the game as a as a pr measure  it's in the game because the people  making the game or at least certain  elements of the game  wanted it there i think i had just been  suspicious that it the leak of the  information  about it might have been more targeted  and with more intent the thing is though  if they were going to leak it  they wouldn't do it through jason  schreyer  because triple a  video game publishers hate  jason schreier because he is one of the  people most consistent  consistently and vehemently writing  about their abuses  when it comes to the work environments  and things like crunch  and hostile workplaces and  some really nasty practices they  hate him if they wanted to leak this  they would not have leaked this  through him and i'm not conspiratorial  enough to go down the path of  ooh maybe that's why he's the perfect  cover he doesn't even know he's being  used i'm like he's been writing about  this for too dang long  he knows how to vet a source i think he  would have sniffed that  if they tried it i think they knew he  would have sniffed that if they were  going to try it which is why at this  point  i don't think it was a deliberate pr  move  that being said while it may not have  been a pr move  from the people at the top  i do find myself wondering about the  motivations for the leak at all and the  timing of the leak  from whatever anonymous individuals  leaked the information  and i have no reason to doubt the  information and  i also find it interesting to start to  think about  how many people on the team actually  would have  known this because as i said  there's almost nothing that would have  to be built  for this to be an option as i said  there's no flat out non-binary option if  there was and like say  they them pronouns were an option that  would have been  so many people would have had to know  because they would have had to have  voice actors record that the writers  would have known  the people lining up the the voice stuff  in the code with the models like they  would have  everybody would have known but  whoever is working on the character  builder  honestly they could have done this  completely on their own  without approval it's actually not  uncommon in video game development  because you have so many  either individuals or small teams  working in isolation on specific parts  it's not uncommon if they have the time  and aren't under crunch  for them to basically kind of fiddle  with something and make what they think  is cool and  then when it eventually gets reviewed  they'll get to find out whether  they get to keep it or not so that  possibility did enter my head that this  might not even have been something  signed off  from people like troy levitt or the  people at the top  this might have just been something that  the character creation team or even  certain individuals within the character  creation team might have decided on  their own  we can do this with the existing assets  we do not need to build anything new for  this we just have to fiddle with code  and unbind a few things  and then part of me wonders if  a reason to leak it  is so that once the public knows  it won't get cut because  if it's leaked and then the game comes  out  next year and that's not the case  well now warner brothers has to answer  to the fact that  there were more options in the character  creation  and they removed it once it's out in the  public  they kind of have to keep it because  removing it  and having that if if they had been able  to mandate hey  that thing you did in there cut no no  cut that and it  had all remained internal  well nobody would have ever known so  it's not  it's it becomes a non-issue it's a  strictly internal issue  whereas if that feature leaks  then the game comes out and the  feature's not there oh  somebody said to cut that  and then that uh that becomes a very  loaded very political  act to do and it's very clear that  warner brothers is trying  so hard to distance themselves from the  politics of jk rowling  when the game was first announced and as  i said it was announced after jk rowling  wrote her  essay in july they they  put out stuff you know official press  release stuff  distancing themselves not only from her  political views  but from her completely basically saying  she is not directly involved in this  game  in any way shape or form so it's very  clear that they are aware  of the problems around jk rowling right  now  especially with how divided her fan base  is however  this is where i have to circle back to  what has become the recurring  subject of this channel lately  which is separating the artist from the  art  what warner brothers wants and what  honestly the developers as well  want us to get in our heads  is that this is not jk rowling's game  they want a disassociation from her  they don't want us to think about her  when we  buy it but even if she is not  creatively involved  any purchase of 